        "original_id": "4025f573-bda6-5543-9aaf-95699b8fa131",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Fancy Free, \"Elvira\", \"Baby Better Start Turnin' 'Em Down\", \"(Now and Then, There's) A Fool Such as I\"\n- People: Dallas Frazier\n- Organizations: The Oak Ridge Boys\n- Topics: album releases, song singles, chart performance\n\nFacts:\n- Fancy Free is the fifth country studio album by The Oak Ridge Boys, and it was released on March 26, 1981.\n- Dallas Frazier wrote the song \"Elvira.\"\n- In 1981, The Oak Ridge Boys made \"Elvira\" a famous country and pop hit, and it became one of their signature songs.\n- The songs \"Elvira,\" \"Baby Better Start Turnin' 'Em Down,\" and \"(Now and Then, There's) A Fool Such as I\" were released as singles.\n- \"Elvira,\" \"Baby Better Start Turnin' 'Em Down,\" and \"(Now and Then, There's) A Fool Such as I\" all failed to chart within the top 40.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
